---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CotFormatter from '../../components/CotFormatter.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Chain-of-Thought Prompt Formatter"
  description="Turn a plain question into a structured reasoning prompt — step-by-step, XML thinking tags, pros/cons, or self-check style."
>
  <CotFormatter client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why structured reasoning prompts work better</h2>
  <p>
    Asking a model to reason before answering — rather than jumping straight
    to a conclusion — consistently improves accuracy on complex questions.
    This tool wraps your task in a few proven reasoning-prompt patterns so
    you don't have to write the scaffolding by hand each time.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Type your task or question.</li>
    <li>Pick a reasoning style that fits — step-by-step for general tasks, XML tags for models like Claude, pros/cons for decisions.</li>
    <li>Copy the formatted prompt and send it to your model.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Chain-of-Thought Prompt FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does this work with every model?</strong> The step-by-step and
    pros/cons styles work broadly. XML thinking tags work especially well
    with Claude, which is trained to respect that structure closely.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
